[h2]Blood Cave wave - the Toxeus champions, and a lot of things that were quietly broken[/h2]

[b]Two bugs that mattered[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Quest items were farmable.[/b] Charon's Oar and the Key of the Warden of Souls could drop from uber bosses cloned from their quest owners. Both closed; the real quest bosses are untouched.
[*][b]Every restored thrown-weapon monster was frozen[/b] - they spawned and then stood there, unable to move or attack. They fight now.
[/list]

[b]Toxeus the Murderer[/b]
[list]
[*][b]The Devourer of Blood[/b] was very nearly unkillable, and not in a good way: he reflected 100% of the damage you dealt, so the stronger your hit, the more likely you killed yourself with it. Reflect cut to 30%, and his pierce resistance from 70% to 40%. He is meaner in exchange - Bloodbath, a low-health Blood Frenzy, and minions of his own.
[*][b]The Endless Hunt[/b] now carries a spear and four skills that are actually his rather than the Enslaver's, hunts without ever losing you, and drops both his soul and his orb - previously he dropped neither.
[*][b]All Toxeus variants[/b] now drop the apex orb, including the two that dropped nothing at all.
[*][b]The green glow[/b] on the Enslaver and his summons is gone. It was baked into the mesh they wore, which is why four earlier attempts at the effects never touched it.
[/list]

[b]Encounters[/b]
[list]
[*]Tantalus the Hunger Unbound fought outside his own den. He is inside it now, and every uber placement was audited so none of them stand in the main walking path.
[*]The Guardians of the General read as uber instead of as trash with red names - larger, with signature skills that fire. Four of those skills were silently aborting because they named animations their skeleton does not have.
[*]Leinth is stronger, has guardians of her own, and her acid attack works - it had never been castable. Killing her opens a way out instead of stranding you.
[/list]

[b]Balance and economy[/b]
[list]
[*][b]The death penalty is cut by 90%[/b], and your tombstone now returns exactly what you lost. It used to return half - in stock Titan Quest too.
[*]Soul drop rates normalised to 33% for non-fixed monsters, 25% for fixed-location bosses. Common trash no longer drops souls at all.
[*]Souls we added now carry their act classification, so the experience-potion forge formulas accept them.
[*]Blade Mastery's description finally tells the truth: it needs a weapon in each hand, one of them a sword, dagger or axe. The bonuses were always gated that way; the text never said so.
[/list]

